      {
        "id": "v2-d8d397-p7-practice-j6-005804-j6-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many whole plots fit in the paddock?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$33$ plots",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{plot}}&=25\\times18=450\\text{ m}^2\\\\N&=15\\,000\\div450\\\\N&=33.3\\ldots\\end{align*}$$Only whole plots fit, so $33$ plots.",
